<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Physician writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-560"}>{"Papers "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-561"}>{"Support "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Send the case "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-560"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"}>{"Case report"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"}>{"Original research article"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"}>{"Physician manuscripts"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"}>{"Clinical literature review"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-561"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"}>{"Research proposal"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"}>{"Literature search & citation"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/customized-writing/"}>{"Customized writing"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-training/"}>{"Physician training"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Clinical Research Protocol and Proposal Writing"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1 className={"h1--long "}>{"Clinical Research Protocol and Proposal Writing"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"What delays an ethics submission is almost never the protocol. It is the participant information sheet written at university reading level, the investigator CV that is two years out of date, the data protection impact assessment nobody knew was needed, or the insurance confirmation that took three weeks to arrive — and each of them costs a whole committee cycle. Pubrica writes clinical research protocols and funder proposals for physicians and surgeons: the protocol itself to SPIRIT 2025 where it is a trial, the full ethics submission set assembled around it, and the funder’s own annexes completed to their format. What we do not do is take the investigator’s responsibility for the submission, because that cannot be outsourced."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#rp-set"}>{"See what your submission needs"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-rp"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-rp"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"One submission at a glance"}</b>{" · an investigator-initiated trial"}</span> <span>{"SPIRIT 2025 · 11 documents"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Protocol written to SPIRIT 2025"}</b><span>{"34 of 34 items"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Information sheet at the reading level asked for"}</b><span>{"Tested"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Sample size with its assumptions stated"}</b><span>{"Justified"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Registration record drafted before enrolment"}</b><span>{"Prospective"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Insurance and CVs chased from day one"}</b><span>{"Not week six"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Idea"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" design "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" protocol "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" the set "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" committee "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"approval"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every protocol"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Design settled first"}</li> <li>{"Sample size justified"}</li> <li>{"Written to SPIRIT 2025"}</li> <li>{"The whole set, not one document"}</li> <li>{"Version-controlled"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $450"}</b><span>{"A structured protocol or proposal, in 10–12 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Protocols, proposals and ethics submissions for clinical teams"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"SPIRIT 2025 · ICH E6(R3)"}</b><span>{"With the Declaration of Helsinki as revised in October 2024"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we offer"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Ten pieces of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Most people need the protocol and two or three of the others. Buying the parts you need is cheaper than buying a package around them."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Design consultation and feasibility"}</b> <span>{"Whether the design can answer the question, what it would take, and what the honest alternatives are if it cannot. Sold as a standalone conversation with a written note and credited against a protocol if you commission one. The single most valuable hour in this service, and the one most often skipped."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Protocol writing"}</b> <span>{"The full protocol to SPIRIT 2025, to ISO 14155 for a device investigation, or to the STROBE items where the study is observational. Typically 25 to 40 pages, version-controlled, with the timeline figure and the schedule of enrolment, interventions and assessments that SPIRIT asks for and that most protocols omit."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Sample size and the statistical analysis plan"}</b> <span>{"The calculation with every assumption stated and its source given, the analysis plan written before any data exists, the primary and secondary outcomes with their estimands, the handling of missing data and the pre-specified subgroups. Our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/free-tools/"} data-nav={""}>{"free sample size calculator"}</a>{" does the arithmetic; what the plan adds is the argument for the assumptions."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Participant information and consent documents"}</b> <span>{"Written in plain language at the reading level your population has, in the committee’s own format, with assent forms where children are involved and a re-consent plan where a participant may reach the age of majority during follow-up. Readability is measured rather than assumed, and it is the commonest reason a committee returns a submission."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"The rest of the ethics submission set"}</b> <span>{"Data management plan, privacy notice and lawful basis, data protection impact assessment where the processing is high risk, case report form, monitoring plan proportionate to the risk, and the covering application itself. Drafted to your instruction and to your committee’s format; the duty and the approval remain yours."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Trial registration"}</b> <span>{"The registration record drafted and ready for you to make public before the first participant is enrolled — CTRI, ClinicalTrials.gov, ISRCTN or the EU Clinical Trials Information System as the jurisdiction requires. Prospective, because retrospective registration is permanently visible and cannot be undone."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Funder proposals and annexes"}</b> <span>{"Written to the funder’s format rather than adapted to it: the NIH package with its Specific Aims page and data management and sharing plan, Horizon Europe against its three scored criteria and their weights, ICMR and DBT on their prescribed forms and budget heads, NIHR with patient and public involvement evidenced rather than asserted."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Budget and cost justification"}</b> <span>{"Built from the protocol rather than estimated against it, so that the staffing follows the visit schedule and the consumables follow the sample count. Justified line by line on the funder’s heads. A budget that does not reconcile to the protocol is the query that most often comes back from a funding committee."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Response to committee and reviewer queries"}</b> <span>{"The query letter answered point by point, with every protocol amendment version-controlled so the committee can see precisely what changed. Most submissions get one, including good ones, and a clear response turns a second meeting into a chair’s action."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Defence slides and protocol-to-manuscript conversion"}</b> <span>{"A presentation for a departmental or funding panel built from the protocol, and later the conversion of the protocol into the methods section of the eventual paper — which is a genuine rewrite, because a protocol is written in the future tense about what will be done and a paper in the past tense about what was."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <nav className={"pagenav"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-who-we-serve-9hfufc"} aria-current={"true"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-our-compliance-140cb45"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-how-it-works-1ld0znq"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-our-experts-7r0rz3"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-sample-work-1vb3563"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-packages-1m7rdti"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-guarantee-1v0o5pb"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-client-stories-1y5zsyi"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-research-proposal-faq-mkbb1p"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-who-we-serve-9hfufc"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions a protocol."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of applicant, and one shared constraint: the committee meets on a fixed date and the clinical work does not pause for it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Physicians and clinician-researchers"}</b><span>{"Investigator-initiated studies designed around a question from practice, where the science is usually sound and the submission set is the unfamiliar part."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Surgeons and interventional specialists"}</b><span>{"Technique and device evaluations, where the comparator question is the hard one and the learning curve has to be in the protocol rather than discovered in the discussion."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Residents, fellows and PhD scholars"}</b><span>{"Often a first submission and usually against a training or thesis deadline. This is where the gap between a thesis protocol and a funder-ready one is widest."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Early-career researchers and postdoctoral fellows"}</b><span>{"Competing for a first independent grant, where the proposal has to do two things at once — make the science convincing and make the applicant look fundable — and the second is usually neglected."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Pharmaceutical and MedTech investigators"}</b><span>{"Sponsored studies and device investigations, where ISO 14155, the MDR and ICH E6(R3) apply alongside the ethics submission, and where the technical documentation is part of the package."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Academic institutions and research units"}</b><span>{"Departments submitting several protocols a year, where a house template and a consistent document set are worth more than any individual submission."}</span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-our-compliance-140cb45"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The four frameworks a protocol is held to."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Two of these changed within the last two years, and one changes again in January 2027. Writing to a superseded version is visible to a reviewer and expensive to correct after submission."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--consort"} role={"img"} aria-label={"SPIRIT 2025"} /></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"SPIRIT 2025 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(the structure of a trial protocol)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Revised in 2025 alongside CONSORT and published simultaneously across five journals. Thirty-four items plus the timeline figure, covering the administrative information, the rationale and objectives, the design, the participants and interventions, the outcomes, the sample size, the allocation and blinding, the data collection and management, the statistical methods, the monitoring, the ethics and dissemination. Writing the protocol to SPIRIT means the eventual CONSORT 2025 paper is already half structured, and the two now share one website at consort-spirit.org."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICH E6(R3)"}>{"ICH"}<em>{"E6(R3) · 2025"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICH E6(R3) "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(good clinical practice, and it has changed)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The Principles and Annex 1 were adopted by ICH and by the CHMP on 23 July 2025 and replace E6(R2) — so a protocol still citing E6(R2) as the current standard is a year out of date. Annex 2, which covers pragmatic and decentralised trial designs, reached Step 4 in June 2026 and applies in the EU from 15 January 2027, with a consolidated version of all three parts published in July 2026. R3 is more proportionate than R2: it asks for quality management built around the risks that actually matter to participants and to the reliability of the results, rather than uniform procedure applied everywhere."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Declaration of Helsinki"}>{"WMA"}<em>{"Helsinki · 2024"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"The Declaration of Helsinki "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(revised October 2024)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Most recently revised at the World Medical Association General Assembly in Helsinki in October 2024, after a thirty-month process. The revision strengthened two areas in particular: participant-centred inclusion, respect and protection — vulnerability, community engagement, global justice, informed consent and the language used about participants — and research beneficence and value, covering scientific rigour and the equitable distribution of benefits, risks and burdens. A protocol that cites the 2013 Fortaleza version as current is citing a superseded document."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--icmje"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICMJE recommendations"} /></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Trial registration "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(prospective, and permanently visible)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The ICMJE requires prospective registration in a WHO primary registry or on ClinicalTrials.gov as a condition of consideration at member journals, and the registration date is public and permanent. Register before the first participant is enrolled, not before submission of the paper: retrospective registration cannot be undone and is a standing reason for a journal to decline. The route follows the jurisdiction — CTRI in India, ISRCTN or ClinicalTrials.gov in the UK alongside HRA approval, ClinicalTrials.gov in the United States, and the EU Clinical Trials Information System under Regulation 536/2014 for trials running in member states."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"A protocol is a commitment, and an ethics committee reads it as one."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A protocol says what will be done to participants and what will be analysed. Every line is something an investigator is committing to and a committee is approving, which makes attribution the point rather than a formality."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Finding precedent language and current guidance. Checking the protocol against SPIRIT and the sponsor’s template. Consistency between the protocol, the analysis plan and the consent documents."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"The scientific rationale; eligibility, endpoints or the analysis approach; anything about risk or consent; and any submission to an ethics committee or funder that the named investigator has not read in full."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-how-it-works-1ld0znq"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the protocol and proposal service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and two of them are about the calendar."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Committees meet monthly, signatures take a fortnight, and insurance confirmations arrive when they arrive. Half of what goes wrong with an ethics submission is scheduling rather than science."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"The question, the design and the calendar"}</h3> <p><b>{"Before anything is quoted."}</b>{" What you want to find out, what design can find it out, and what the real dates are — the committee’s meeting and paper deadline, the funder’s call, the date the fellow leaves. This is also where we say if the design cannot answer the question, which is unwelcome in week one and cheaper than at review."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"Objectives, hypotheses and the sample size"}</h3> <p><b>{"Objectives numbered and testable, and the sample size justified rather than asserted."}</b>{" Every assumption stated: the expected effect and where that expectation comes from, the variance, the allowance for attrition, the significance level and the power. A committee can then disagree with an assumption, which is a conversation, instead of with a bare number, which is a query letter."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"The protocol, written to its structure"}</h3> <p><b>{"SPIRIT 2025 for a trial, ISO 14155 for a device investigation, the STROBE items as the anchor for observational work."}</b>{" Background and rationale, design, participants, interventions, outcomes with their instruments and time points, data collection, the statistical analysis plan, monitoring, and dissemination. Version number and date on every page, because amendments have to be traceable."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"The rest of the set, in parallel"}</h3> <p><b>{"Participant information sheet, consent form, assent where children are involved, data management plan, case report form, privacy notice."}</b>{" Written alongside the protocol rather than after it, and checked against each other — the commonest committee query of all is that the information sheet describes a different study from the protocol, usually because the design changed and only one document was updated."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Funder annexes and registration"}</h3> <p><b>{"The funder’s own format, their budget heads, their page limits and their scoring criteria."}</b>{" An NIH Specific Aims page, a Horizon Europe impact section, an ICMR budget on the prescribed heads, an NIHR plain English summary that is genuinely plain. And the registration record drafted ready to be made public before the first participant is enrolled."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Second review, then the query letter"}</h3> <p><b>{"Read by somebody who did not write it, against the committee’s own checklist."}</b>{" Then, when the query letter arrives — and it usually does, even for good submissions — the response drafted point by point, with every protocol amendment version-controlled so that the committee can see exactly what changed between submission and resubmission."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the idea. We will tell you what it takes."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Two business days, at no cost: whether the design can answer the question, what the submission set will contain in your jurisdiction, how long it takes to assemble, and whether your committee date is realistic. That last answer has saved clients a full meeting cycle more than once."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The question"}</b><span>{"In a sentence, however rough"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The setting"}</b><span>{"Which sites, which population, what is routine there"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The dates"}</b><span>{"Committee deadline, funder call, and when staff change"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The committee"}</b><span>{"Their forms, their format and their meeting calendar"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Prior work"}</b><span>{"Pilot data, an audit, anything that supports feasibility"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The team"}</b><span>{"Who does what, and who signs"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"Send the committee’s own forms and guidance notes at the start. Every ethics committee has a house format, most publish it, and almost nobody reads it before writing. A protocol written to a generic template and then forced into a local form is where inconsistencies between documents come from — and inconsistency between the protocol and the information sheet is the query committees raise most."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What the submission actually contains"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"A protocol is one document. A submission is a folder."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Most first-time applicants write an excellent protocol and then discover, four weeks before the meeting, that the committee also wants six or nine other things — several of which have to come from people who are on leave. The builder below assembles the set from your study and your jurisdiction, says roughly how long it takes to put together, and tells you whether your date is real."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"rp-set"} data-tool={"pro"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"rp-set-body"}>{"Ethics submission set builder"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"Every document your committee will ask for, the registration route for your region, the annexes your funder adds, and whether your date holds."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"rp-set-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-rp-kind"}>{"What kind of study?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"kind"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-rp-kind"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"trial"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Interventional trial"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"dev"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Device investigation"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"obs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Observational study"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"sec"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Secondary or routine data"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"qual"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Qualitative research"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Where the approval comes from"}</span><select data-k={"reg"}><option value={"in"} selected={true}>{"India — institutional ethics committee"}</option><option value={"uk"}>{"United Kingdom — HRA and a Research Ethics Committee"}</option><option value={"us"}>{"United States — an IRB under the Common Rule"}</option><option value={"eu"}>{"European Union — national authority and ethics committee"}</option><option value={"oth"}>{"Elsewhere"}</option></select></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Who is funding it"}</span><select data-k={"fund"}><option value={"none"} selected={true}>{"Unfunded, or departmental"}</option><option value={"icmr"}>{"ICMR"}</option><option value={"dbt"}>{"DBT or DST"}</option><option value={"nih"}>{"NIH"}</option><option value={"nihr"}>{"NIHR"}</option><option value={"heu"}>{"Horizon Europe"}</option><option value={"ind"}>{"An industry sponsor"}</option><option value={"chy"}>{"A charity or foundation"}</option></select></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Weeks until the submission deadline"}</span><em>{"The committee’s date, not the one you told your department."}</em><input type={"number"} data-k={"weeks"} value={"8"} step={1} min={1} /></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"drug"} /><span>{"A medicinal product is being given or withheld"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"dev"} /><span>{"A medical device is being investigated"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"minor"} /><span>{"Children, or adults who may lack capacity, are included"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"ident"} checked={true} /><span>{"Identifiable personal data will be processed"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"bio"} /><span>{"Biological samples will be collected or stored"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"9 documents, not one"}</b><span>{"about 8 weeks to assemble"}</span></div><div className={"tbig tbig--3"}><div className={"tbig__i"}><p className={"tbig__v"}>{"9"}</p><p className={"tbig__l"}>{"Items in the submission set"}</p></div><div className={"tbig__i"}><p className={"tbig__v"}>{"8"}<small>{" wk"}</small></p><p className={"tbig__l"}>{"To assemble and write"}</p></div><div className={"tbig__i"}><p className={"tbig__v"}><span className={"tflag tflag--mid"}>{"Tight"}</span></p><p className={"tbig__l"}>{"Against your date"}</p></div></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Structural guideline: SPIRIT 2025."}</b>{" SPIRIT was revised in 2025 alongside CONSORT and now runs to 34 items plus the timeline figure. It is the protocol counterpart of CONSORT, it shares one website with it at consort-spirit.org, and writing the protocol to SPIRIT means the eventual CONSORT paper is already half structured."}</p><p><b>{"Your timeline."}</b>{" Tight. 8 weeks against roughly 8. It holds only if the institutional signatures and the insurance confirmation are chased from day one rather than at the end."}</p></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"The submission set"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"The protocol itself"}</b><span>{"Written to SPIRIT 2025, with the version number and date on every page. Committees reject on version control more often than anyone expects, because an amendment referring to an unnumbered protocol cannot be traced."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Participant information sheet"}</b><span>{"In plain language, at the reading level your population actually has rather than the one the template assumes. This is the document committees return most often, and almost always for readability rather than content."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Informed consent form"}</b><span>{"Separate from the information sheet, signed and dated by participant and investigator, with a copy for the participant. The investigator holds responsibility for the consent process; we draft the document, we do not take the duty."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Investigator CV and site details"}</b><span>{"Current, signed and dated, for every site. Out-of-date CVs are a routine cause of a query letter and a four-week delay."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Case report form or data collection tool"}</b><span>{"Submitted with the protocol, because a committee reads it to check that you are not collecting more than the protocol justifies."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Data management and monitoring plan"}</b><span>{"Who holds the data, where, for how long, who may access it and what happens at the end. Proportionate to the study: a trial needs a monitoring plan, a notes review does not."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Data protection documentation"}</b><span>{"A privacy notice, the lawful basis for processing, and — where the processing is likely to be high risk — a data protection impact assessment. In the UK and EU this is a GDPR obligation on the sponsor, not a form for the ethics committee, and it is frequently the item that is missing on the day."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Trial registration record"}</b><span>{"Completed and public before the first participant is enrolled. Retrospective registration is permanently visible in the registry and is a standing reason for journals to decline the eventual paper."}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Insurance and indemnity"}</b><span>{"Proof of cover appropriate to the risk. Usually institutional, occasionally not, and almost always the item nobody chases until the week of the meeting."}</span></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"Registration"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Clinical Trials Registry – India (CTRI)"}</b><span>{"Registration before enrolment of the first participant is required by the CTRI and expected by Indian journals. ICMR-funded work is registered regardless of design."}</span></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"What your funder adds"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Funder-specific annexes"}</b><span>{"No funder annexes. The ethics submission still needs a budget or a statement that the study is unfunded, because a committee reads cost as a feasibility question."}</span></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"How this was worked out, and what it is not."}</b>{" The set is built from the design and the jurisdiction you selected. Structural guidelines: SPIRIT 2025 for trial protocols at consort-spirit.org, ISO 14155 for device clinical investigation plans, STROBE and RECORD as anchors for observational and routine-data studies, SRQR or COREQ for qualitative work. Good clinical practice is ICH E6(R3): its Principles and Annex 1 were adopted by ICH and the CHMP on 23 July 2025 and replace E6(R2), and Annex 2, covering pragmatic and decentralised designs, reached Step 4 in June 2026 and applies in the EU from 15 January 2027. The ethical framework is the Declaration of Helsinki, most recently revised at the World Medical Association General Assembly in Helsinki in October 2024. "}<b>{"This is a planning aid, not regulatory advice, and it is not exhaustive."}</b>{" Your ethics committee, your competent authority and your institution set the actual requirements, and they differ. "}<b>{"The investigator and the sponsor hold responsibility for the ethics submission and for the consent process."}</b>{" We draft documents to your instruction; we do not take that duty, and no writing service can."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Whose responsibility the ethics submission is"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The investigator’s, and the sponsor’s. This needs saying plainly because informed consent forms and risk-benefit analyses are routinely offered without anybody saying who owns them, and that ambiguity is a real exposure for a client rather than a drafting convenience. So: we write documents to your instruction and to the committee’s format. The scientific and ethical content is yours, the approval is granted to you, and the consent process — the conversation with the participant, the judgement about capacity, the decision that this person has understood — is a clinical act that belongs to the investigator and cannot be bought from anybody. What a writing service can properly do is make the documents clear, complete and consistent with each other, which is where submissions actually fail. What it cannot do is hold the duty. Any supplier offering to take it is describing something they are not able to do."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Six situations, and what each one turns on"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What the work actually looks like."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"These are the six commonest shapes this work takes. In each, one thing decides whether the submission goes through first time, and it is rarely the thing the applicant is worrying about."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"A cardiologist preparing an investigator-initiated trial"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The protocol is written to SPIRIT 2025 and the science is usually sound. What decides it is the sample size: a committee reads an unjustified number as a feasibility risk, because a trial that cannot recruit its target exposes participants to research that cannot answer its question. The calculation goes in with every assumption stated — the expected effect, where that expectation comes from, the variance, the attrition allowance — so that a reviewer can disagree with the assumption rather than with the number. The second thing is the monitoring plan: an investigator-initiated trial still needs one, proportionate to risk, and applicants routinely omit it because no sponsor asked."}</p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"An orthopaedic surgeon evaluating a technique"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The hard question is what the comparator is. Comparing a new technique against your own historical series is a before-and-after comparison in one centre, confounded by the learning curve, by case selection and by everything else that changed in the intervening years. A committee will ask, and the honest answers are a concurrent comparison, a prospective registry with pre-specified outcomes, or an explicit acknowledgement that the design supports a hypothesis rather than a conclusion. The learning curve also has to be in the protocol as a stated factor, not discovered in the discussion."}</p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"An ENT specialist submitting a device study"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"This is a different document from a clinical trial protocol. A clinical investigation plan is written to ISO 14155, it sits alongside the risk analysis to ISO 14971 and the instructions for use, and under the EU MDR it goes to a competent authority as well as an ethics committee. Applicants who write it as an academic protocol are asked for the technical documentation they did not know formed part of the submission, and the delay is measured in months rather than weeks."}</p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"A resident turning a thesis into a funder-ready protocol"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"A thesis protocol is written to satisfy a supervisor and a university committee; a funder’s is written to compete. The differences are structural: the background compresses to a page that establishes a gap rather than demonstrating reading, the objectives become testable and are numbered, the methods acquire a timeline and a budget, and a feasibility case appears that a thesis never needed. It is a rewrite rather than a reformat, and it is best done before the thesis version is finalised rather than after."}</p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"A neurologist proposing an observational cohort"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"There is no SPIRIT for observational studies, which is why they are so often under-specified and why committees query them more than trials. The protocol is written against the STROBE items so that the decisions are made now rather than during analysis: how confounders will be selected and on what basis, how missing data will be handled, which analyses are pre-specified and which are exploratory, and what the follow-up window actually is. A pre-specified analysis plan is what separates a cohort study from a fishing expedition, and committees can tell."}</p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"A dental surgeon proposing a public health intervention"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Community and behavioural interventions bring consent questions that individual clinical research does not: who consents when the unit of allocation is a school, a clinic or a village, what happens to people in the setting who did not consent, and how the intervention is withdrawn if it turns out to work. These are answerable, and answering them in the protocol rather than in a query response is the difference between one committee meeting and three."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-our-experts-7r0rz3"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-sample-work-1vb3563"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The four pages a committee reads closely."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A committee does not read a forty-page protocol line by line. It reads the sample size justification, the information sheet, the consistency between documents, and the risk-benefit statement — and it queries on those four. Use the tabs, then open the full sample below to read a complete protocol summary on this page."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Protocol package · extract"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Investigator-initiated trial · SPIRIT 2025 · 11 documents"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"Sample size · the information sheet · consistency · risk and benefit"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the protocol package"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"rp-t1"} aria-controls={"rp-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Sample size"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"rp-t2"} aria-controls={"rp-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Information sheet"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"rp-t3"} aria-controls={"rp-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Consistency"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"rp-t4"} aria-controls={"rp-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Risk"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"rp-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"rp-t1"}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The number"}</dt><dd>{"212 participants, 106 per arm, before attrition. The number is the least important line in this section."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Expected effect, and where it comes from"}</dt><dd>{"A difference of 0.45 standard deviations, taken from two named published trials in a comparable population, with both cited. Not “a clinically meaningful difference”, which means nothing a reviewer can check."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Why that effect and not a larger one"}</dt><dd>{"Because the smallest difference worth detecting is a clinical judgement and has to be argued. Powering for a large effect is how a trial ends up unable to exclude a small but important one."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Variance assumption"}</dt><dd>{"Standard deviation taken from the same published trials, with a note that the local population may differ and how that would be handled."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Attrition"}</dt><dd>{"15%, justified from the site’s own follow-up rates in a comparable study rather than from a convention. Inflated figure: 250."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Alpha, power and sidedness"}</dt><dd>{"5% two-sided, 90% power, all stated. One-sided testing is occasionally right and always has to be defended."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Feasibility, checked against the clinic"}</dt><dd>{"250 participants over 18 months at this site means 14 a month against a clinic that sees 41 eligible patients a month. Stated, with the consent rate assumption given, because a committee reads an unchecked recruitment target as a risk to participants."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"rp-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"rp-t2"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“You will be randomised in a 1:1 ratio to one of two arms”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Three technical words in one sentence, none of them explained. Rewritten as: “A computer will decide, by chance, which of the two treatments you get. Each has an equal chance. Neither you nor your doctor can choose.”"}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“There is no direct therapeutic benefit to participation”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"True, and unreadable. Rewritten as: “Taking part may not help you. We are doing this study to find out whether this treatment helps people in future.” Committees insist on this being unambiguous, and softening it is a real ethical problem rather than a stylistic one."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Withdrawal explained in one clause at the end"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Moved up and given its own short section: that you can stop at any time, that you do not have to give a reason, and that your care will not change. This is the paragraph participants most want and template sheets most often bury."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Reading level measured at grade 13"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Rewritten to grade 7 as measured by SMOG, against the target the committee specified. The instrument and the target are both recorded in the submission, because “written in plain language” is an assertion and a measured grade is not."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"What happens to your samples, in its own section"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"With separate optional consent for storage and future unspecified research, which cannot be bundled into the main consent."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Rewritten from grade 13 to grade 7"}</span><span>{"The commonest reason a submission comes back"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"rp-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"rp-t3"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Follow-up: 12 months in the protocol, 6 in the information sheet"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The design was extended in draft four and only the protocol was updated. This is the single most common cross-document error we find, and the one committees most reliably catch."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Blood volume: 20 ml in the protocol, 15 ml on the consent form"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"A participant consents to what the form says. Reconciled to 20 ml in both, with the number of draws and the total across the study stated in the information sheet."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Data retention: 5 years in the privacy notice, 10 in the data management plan"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Reconciled to the institution’s own retention policy, which is what the committee will compare both against."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Secondary outcomes: 6 in the protocol, 4 in the registration draft"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Reconciled before registration, because the registered record becomes the reference against which the eventual paper is checked for outcome switching."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Every document version-numbered and dated"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"So that an amendment can be traced. Committees query unnumbered protocols routinely and applicants are consistently surprised by it."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"4 inconsistencies, all from one design change"}</span><span>{"Caught before submission, not in the query letter"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"rp-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"rp-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Risks, listed individually"}</dt><dd>{"Each with its likelihood, its severity and what will be done about it. Not a paragraph saying risks are minimal."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Procedures beyond routine care"}</dt><dd>{"Named explicitly and separated from what the participant would have had anyway, because that distinction is the whole of the burden question."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Burden in hours"}</dt><dd>{"Six extra visits, roughly forty minutes each, plus travel. Quantified, because “minimal additional burden” is the applicant’s judgement rather than the participant’s."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Benefit, stated honestly"}</dt><dd>{"Including where there is none to the participant. The Declaration of Helsinki, as revised in October 2024, puts particular weight on the equitable distribution of benefits, risks and burdens."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Stopping rules"}</dt><dd>{"What would cause the trial to stop early, who decides, and on what data. A trial without stopping rules is a trial that cannot respond to harm."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What happens after it ends"}</dt><dd>{"Whether participants who benefited continue to have access, and how results will be returned to them. Increasingly asked for, and rarely present in a first draft."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · study and site details changed"}</span><span>{"Second-reader review, before submission"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"A committee reads four things closely and queries on all four. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The consistency tab is the one that surprises applicants."}</b>{" Four inconsistencies between documents, all of them produced by a single design change in draft four that was applied to the protocol and to nothing else. None of them is a mistake anybody made; they are what happens when eleven documents are written by four people over six weeks and only one gets updated."}</p> <p><b>{"The information sheet is the commonest reason a submission comes back."}</b>{" Not content — readability. A sheet written at grade 13 describing a study to a population that reads at grade 7 has not obtained informed consent, it has obtained a signature, and committees increasingly say so."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Sample size justified, not asserted"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Every assumption stated with its source."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Readability measured, not claimed"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With the instrument and the target recorded."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Documents checked against each other"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Which is where a design change goes to hide."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Risk quantified in hours and visits"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Because “minimal burden” is the applicant’s judgement."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a protocol package built round a study like yours — same design, same jurisdiction, same committee format."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-rp"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-rp"}>{"Read the full protocol summary"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-rp"}> <span><b>{"Read the full protocol summary"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the design, the outcomes, the sample size, the SPIRIT schedule, the document set and the second-reader findings"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-rp"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Research proposal · sample protocol summary"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Protocol summary and submission set — investigator-initiated trial"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A real protocol package with the condition, the intervention, the institution and every identifying detail changed. The structure, the second-reader findings and the document list are as delivered. Ask us and we will send one built around a study like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"Design, in the terms SPIRIT asks for"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"SPIRIT element"}</th><th>{"As written"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Design"}</td><td>{"Parallel-group, two-arm, 1:1, superiority. Named explicitly rather than left to be inferred from the methods, which SPIRIT asks for and most protocols skip."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Setting"}</td><td>{"Two sites, both secondary care, with what constitutes usual care at each described — because it differs, and undeclared differences in usual care are the commonest source of unexplained variation."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Eligibility"}</td><td>{"Nine inclusion and six exclusion criteria, each operationalised. “Significant comorbidity” replaced with a defined index and a threshold, because a criterion a screening nurse cannot apply is not a criterion."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Interventions"}</td><td>{"Dose, route, schedule, duration, who administers, what counts as a protocol deviation, and the criteria for discontinuing or modifying."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Primary outcome"}</td><td>{"One. Its measurement instrument, the time point, and who assesses it — blinded to allocation, which matters because the outcome is subjective."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Secondary outcomes"}</td><td>{"Six, ranked, each with instrument and time point. Ranked now, because the registered record is what the eventual paper is checked against for outcome switching."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Allocation"}</td><td>{"Computer-generated sequence, stratified by site, in permuted blocks of varying size. Concealment by a central web system, described — this is two sentences and it is the first thing a methods reviewer looks for."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Blinding"}</td><td>{"Participants, outcome assessors and the analyst; the treating clinician cannot be blinded, and that is stated with what is done to limit its effect rather than left out."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Timeline figure"}</td><td>{"The SPIRIT schedule of enrolment, interventions and assessments, as a figure. Frequently omitted, and it is the item that makes the visit burden legible to a committee at a glance."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"Sample size, with the workings"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Assumption"}</th><th>{"Value"}</th><th>{"Where it came from"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Smallest difference worth detecting"}</td><td>{"0.45 SD"}</td><td>{"Two named published trials in a comparable population, both cited. Argued as a clinical judgement rather than presented as a fact."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Standard deviation"}</td><td>{"From the same trials"}</td><td>{"With a note that the local population may differ and what would be done if the observed variance were larger."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Alpha"}</td><td>{"5%, two-sided"}</td><td>{"Stated. One-sided testing is occasionally correct and always needs defending."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Power"}</td><td>{"90%"}</td><td>{"Stated, with the consequence of 80% given for comparison so the committee can see the trade."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Analysable sample"}</td><td>{"212 (106 per arm)"}</td><td>{"The output of the calculation, which is the least important line in the section."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Attrition allowance"}</td><td>{"15%"}</td><td>{"From the site’s own follow-up rates in a comparable study, not from convention."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Target recruitment"}</td><td>{"250"}</td><td>{"Inflated figure."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Feasibility check"}</td><td>{"14 per month for 18 months"}</td><td>{"Against a clinic seeing 41 eligible patients a month, with the assumed consent rate stated. A committee reads an unchecked recruitment target as a risk to participants, not as optimism."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"The submission set, as filed"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"#"}</th><th>{"Document"}</th><th>{"Note"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"1"}</td><td>{"Protocol, v1.3, dated"}</td><td>{"SPIRIT 2025, 34 items, version and date in the footer of every page."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"2"}</td><td>{"Participant information sheet, v1.3"}</td><td>{"Rewritten from grade 13 to grade 7 as measured by SMOG, against the committee’s stated target."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"3"}</td><td>{"Informed consent form, v1.3"}</td><td>{"Separate document, with a copy for the participant and a separate optional section for sample storage."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"4"}</td><td>{"GP or usual-clinician notification letter"}</td><td>{"Required by this committee and routinely forgotten by applicants."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"5"}</td><td>{"Case report form"}</td><td>{"Submitted with the protocol, because the committee checks that the data collected is no more than the protocol justifies."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"6"}</td><td>{"Data management plan"}</td><td>{"Who holds what, where, for how long, and what happens at the end."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"7"}</td><td>{"Privacy notice and lawful basis"}</td><td>{"Plus a data protection impact assessment, because the processing is high risk."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"8"}</td><td>{"Monitoring plan"}</td><td>{"Proportionate to the risk. Investigator-initiated trials still need one and frequently arrive without."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"9"}</td><td>{"Investigator CVs, current and signed"}</td><td>{"For both sites. Out-of-date CVs cost a query letter and a meeting cycle."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"10"}</td><td>{"Insurance and indemnity confirmation"}</td><td>{"Chased from week one. It took eleven days to arrive, which is why."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"11"}</td><td>{"Registration record, drafted"}</td><td>{"Ready to be made public before the first participant is enrolled. Prospective, permanently visible, and not undoable."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Second-reader findings, before submission"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Finding"}</th><th>{"Severity"}</th><th>{"Resolution"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Follow-up stated as 12 months in the protocol and 6 in the information sheet"}</td><td>{"Critical"}</td><td>{"Design extended in draft four; only the protocol updated. Reconciled to 12 across all documents."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Blood volume 20 ml in the protocol, 15 ml on the consent form"}</td><td>{"Critical"}</td><td>{"A participant consents to what the form says. Reconciled to 20 ml, with the number of draws and the study total added to the information sheet."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Six secondary outcomes in the protocol, four in the registration draft"}</td><td>{"Major"}</td><td>{"Reconciled before registration. The registered record is the reference for outcome switching."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Data retention 5 years in one document, 10 in another"}</td><td>{"Major"}</td><td>{"Reconciled to the institution’s retention policy, which the committee compares both against."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Information sheet at grade 13"}</td><td>{"Major"}</td><td>{"Rewritten to grade 7 with the instrument and target recorded in the submission."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“Significant comorbidity” as an exclusion criterion"}</td><td>{"Minor"}</td><td>{"Replaced with a defined index and threshold. A criterion a screening nurse cannot apply is not a criterion."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"No stopping rules"}</td><td>{"Major"}</td><td>{"Added, with who decides and on what data. A trial without them cannot respond to harm."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Seven findings, none of them a failure of competence. Six of the seven came from one design change midway through drafting, applied to some documents and not others. That is what a second reader is for, and it is why the read is done by somebody who did not write the package."}</p> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"What this package does not do"}</h4> <p>{"It does not obtain your approval, and it does not carry your responsibility. The investigator and the sponsor hold the duty for the ethics submission and for the conduct of the consent process — the conversation with the participant, the judgement about capacity, the decision that this person has genuinely understood. That is a clinical act and it cannot be bought from a writing service."}</p> <p>{"It also does not guarantee a first-time approval. Most submissions receive a query letter, including good ones, and a committee that asks nothing is unusual rather than reassuring. What a well-assembled package does is make the queries substantive instead of administrative, which is the difference between a chair’s action and another full meeting."}</p> <div className={"fsm__foot"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-research-proposal-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-packages-1m7rdti"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three tiers, and the add-ons priced separately."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Priced on the design, the jurisdiction and how much of the submission set you need. Every figure is a floor with its cap beside it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Basic"}</span> <h3>{"The protocol, written"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Residents, fellows and academic researchers with a settled topic and a design already chosen"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $450"}</b><span>{"25–30 pages · 1 site · 1 revision round"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"10–12 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The protocol structured to SPIRIT 2025, or to the STROBE items where observational"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Background, rationale, objectives and methodology"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Referencing in APA, AMA or Vancouver, and language editing"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Originality screening, with every match classified"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Version control set up, so amendments stay traceable"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: sample size; the ethics document set; registration."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-rp"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-rp"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Basic"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"With the design and the statistics"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Clinicians and early-career faculty who need the methodology and the analysis settled, not just written down"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $700"}</b><span>{"1 study · sample size and analysis plan · 2 sites"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"12–15 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Basic"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Design consultation: whether the design can answer the question"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Hypotheses, variables and outcome instruments with their time points"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Sample size with every assumption stated and its source given"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A statistical analysis plan written before any data exists"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Alignment to ICH E6(R3) and to your committee’s own format"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: the full ethics set; funder annexes; the budget."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-rp"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-rp"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Advanced"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Premium"}</span> <h3>{"The whole submission set"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Physicians and surgeons preparing for ethics review, an investigator-initiated trial or a funding call"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,100"}</b><span>{"up to 11 documents · 1 committee · 1 funder format"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15–20 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Advanced"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Participant information sheet and consent form, readability measured against a target"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Data management plan, privacy notice and impact assessment where needed"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Case report form, monitoring plan and the covering application"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Registration record drafted, ready before first enrolment"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Second-reader review across the whole set for cross-document consistency"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Two further revision rounds, and the response to the committee’s query letter"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Multi-site and multi-country submissions are quoted separately."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-rp"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-rp"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Premium"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"psv rv rv-d2"}> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"Single service"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"Grant budget and cost justification"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"From $150"}</b><span>{"5 business days"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Bought on its own, or alongside any tier"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Built from the protocol rather than estimated against it, so the staffing follows the visit schedule and the consumables follow the sample count. Justified line by line on the funder’s own heads."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"Single service"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"PICO or PICO-T framing"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"From $75"}</b><span>{"3 business days"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Bought on its own, or alongside any tier"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"The question made searchable and testable, with the population, intervention, comparator, outcome and time frame each operationalised so a screening nurse or a database could apply them."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"Single service"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"Defence or panel slide deck"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"From $120"}</b><span>{"4–5 business days"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Bought on its own, or alongside any tier"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Built from the protocol, with speaker notes and the three slides a panel will stop on: the design, the sample size justification and the feasibility case."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"Single service"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"Committee query response"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"From $180"}</b><span>{"5–7 business days"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Bought on its own, or alongside any tier"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"Point by point, with every protocol amendment version-controlled so the committee can see exactly what changed. Turns a second full meeting into a chair’s action."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"Single service"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"Scientific translation into English"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"From $100"}</b><span>{"Quoted on length"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Bought on its own, or alongside any tier"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"By a subject-matter translator and then edited as a document rather than merely rendered, because clinical terminology that is standard in one language often has no single equivalent in another."}</p> </div> <div className={"psv__i"}> <p className={"psv__k"}>{"Single service"}</p> <p className={"psv__n"}>{"Protocol to manuscript conversion"}</p> <p className={"psv__p"}><b>{"From $250"}</b><span>{"7–10 business days"}</span></p> <p className={"psv__t"}>{"Bought on its own, or alongside any tier"}</p> <p className={"psv__d"}>{"A genuine rewrite: a protocol is written in the future tense about what will be done, a paper in the past tense about what was, and the two differ in more than the verbs."}</p> </div> </div> <p className={"psv__foot rv rv-d2"}><b>{"Expedited delivery at 5–7 business days is available where capacity allows, and is quoted on capacity rather than on urgency."}</b>{" We will not charge you more for the same work because your date is close, and where a date is not achievable we will tell you rather than take the fee and miss it."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-guarantee-1v0o5pb"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A committee’s decision and a funder’s decision both belong to somebody else. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the protocol and the set meet the brief and the committee’s format, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed, and the response to the first query letter included on the Premium tier."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The query letter is expected"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Most submissions get one, including good ones. Answering it is part of the Premium tier rather than a new engagement, because the job is approval rather than a document."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A SPIRIT item missed, a cross-document inconsistency, a form filled in the wrong version — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Told early if the date will not hold"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Committee deadlines do not move and neither do funding calls. If your date is not achievable you hear it at the quote stage rather than in week five."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Version control from day one"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Every document numbered and dated, so that an amendment can be traced and a committee can see exactly what changed. It sounds administrative and it prevents the commonest query."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" The investigator and the sponsor hold responsibility for the ethics submission, for the conduct of the study and for the consent process. We draft documents to your instruction; we do not take that duty, and no writing service can. We cannot guarantee ethics approval or a funding award, and we will not quote a success rate as though we could — those decisions belong to a committee and a panel. We will not write a protocol for a study we think cannot answer its question; we will say so, explain why, and set out what would. We will not write a sample size justification backwards from a number that suits the recruitment you can manage, and where the achievable sample is smaller than the question needs we will tell you what that means for what the study can conclude. And we will not draft a consent document that softens a statement about benefit, because that is not a stylistic preference."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"The feasibility answer is free"}</p> <p>{"Whether the design can answer the question, what the submission set contains in your jurisdiction, how long it takes to assemble and whether your committee date is realistic. Two business days, no cost, no obligation. The date answer alone has saved clients a full meeting cycle, which in most institutions is four to eight weeks."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Registration before enrolment"}</p> <p>{"We draft the registration record early and remind you to make it public before the first participant is enrolled, because that is the only moment at which it can be done. Retrospective registration is permanently visible in the registry, it cannot be corrected, and it is a standing reason for an ICMJE member journal to decline the eventual paper — years later, when nothing can be done about it."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Confidentiality and data handling"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves. Unpublished protocols, pilot data and funding applications are held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, kept only as long as the project needs them, never used to train anything and never shared outside your project team. Competing applications to the same call are never taken."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Versions checked, every project"}</p> <p>{"Frameworks in this area move. ICH E6(R3) replaced E6(R2) in July 2025, its Annex 2 for pragmatic and decentralised designs applies in the EU from January 2027, SPIRIT was revised in 2025, and the Declaration of Helsinki was revised in October 2024. We check the current version at the start of each project rather than carrying a list over from the last one, and where we find a citation of ours that has gone stale we say so rather than quietly correcting it."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-client-stories-1y5zsyi"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three submissions, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named client has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Four of our eleven documents disagreed with each other. All four came from one design change that only got applied to the protocol.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CLINICAL"}<br />{"TRIAL"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Ethics"}<br />{"Submission"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Consultant cardiologist · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Submitted as"}</b><span>{"Investigator-initiated trial"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They told me at the quote stage that my committee date was not achievable. I did not want to hear it and it was correct.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"SURGICAL"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Protocol"}<br />{"Package"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Orthopaedic surgeon · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Submitted as"}</b><span>{"Technique evaluation"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Our information sheet tested at grade thirteen. We had all read it and none of us noticed, because we could read it.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}><span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}><span className={"mcov__k"}>{"PUBLIC"}<br />{"HEALTH"}</span><span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Community"}<br />{"Intervention"}</span><span className={"mcov__r"} /></span></span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Public health physician · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Submitted as"}</b><span>{"Cluster intervention study"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-research-proposal-faq-mkbb1p"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Protocol and proposal FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Nine questions applicants ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure whether your design can answer your question, or what your committee will ask for? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-0"}><span>{"What should be included in a clinical research protocol?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"For a trial, the 34 items of SPIRIT 2025 plus its timeline figure: administrative information with the registration details and the version, the background and rationale, the objectives, the design named explicitly, the setting and eligibility criteria as they will actually be applied, the interventions with their dose, route, schedule and discontinuation criteria, the outcomes with their instruments and time points, the sample size with its assumptions, recruitment, allocation and concealment, blinding, data collection and management, the statistical methods, monitoring and harms reporting, and the ethics and dissemination plans. The two items applicants most often omit are the schedule of enrolment, interventions and assessments — which SPIRIT asks for as a figure and which is what makes the visit burden legible to a committee at a glance — and the stopping rules. For observational studies there is no SPIRIT, which is why they are so often under-specified; write the protocol against the STROBE items instead, because that forces the decisions that otherwise get made during analysis."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-1"}><span>{"How do I justify my sample size?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"By stating every assumption and where it came from, not by producing a number. A committee or a reviewer cannot disagree with 212; they can disagree with a 0.45 standard deviation effect taken from two named trials in a different population, and that is a conversation rather than a query letter. So: the smallest difference worth detecting, argued as a clinical judgement with its source; the variance and where it came from; the significance level and whether the test is one- or two-sided, with a defence if it is one-sided; the power; the allowance for attrition, justified from your own site’s figures rather than from convention. Then the feasibility check, which is the part that is usually missing: if the inflated target is 250 over eighteen months at a clinic seeing 41 eligible patients a month, say so and state the consent rate you are assuming. A committee reads an unchecked recruitment target as a risk to participants, because a trial that cannot recruit exposes people to research that cannot answer its question. Our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/free-tools/"} data-nav={""}>{"free sample size calculator"}</a>{" does the arithmetic; what the protocol adds is the argument."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-2"}><span>{"Why did my ethics submission come back?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Most submissions get a query letter, including good ones, and a committee that asks nothing is unusual rather than reassuring. But the queries cluster, and four causes account for most of them. The participant information sheet is written above the reading level of the population — this is the single commonest, and it is a real ethical point rather than a stylistic one, because a sheet nobody can read has obtained a signature rather than consent. Two documents disagree, usually because the design changed and only one was updated. The sample size is a number without a justification. And something administrative is missing or stale: an unsigned CV, an unnumbered protocol version, an insurance confirmation that has not arrived. Three of those four are entirely preventable by a second reader going through the set against the committee’s own checklist before submission, which takes a day and saves a meeting cycle."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-3"}><span>{"Will you write my informed consent form?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"We will draft the document to your instruction and to your committee’s format, and we will measure its readability against a stated target rather than asserting that it is in plain language. What we will not do, and what no writing service can do, is take the responsibility. The investigator and the sponsor hold the duty for the ethics submission, and the consent "}<i>{"process"}</i>{" — the conversation with the participant, the judgement about capacity, the decision that this person has genuinely understood what they are agreeing to — is a clinical act. It belongs to the clinician taking consent and it cannot be bought. We say this plainly because consent forms and risk-benefit analyses are routinely drafted without anybody stating who owns them, and that ambiguity is a real exposure for a client rather than a convenience. Where a document is drafted by us, the covering application says so, exactly as an acknowledgement in a paper would."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-4"}><span>{"What is the difference between a research proposal and a protocol?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"A protocol is the operating document: what will be done, to whom, when, by whom, and what happens when something goes wrong. Its readers are an ethics committee, a regulator and, later, the study team itself. A proposal is a competitive document: why this question matters, why this team, why now, and what it will cost. Its readers are a funding panel scoring against published criteria. They share a methods section and differ in almost everything else — the proposal compresses the background into a page that establishes a gap rather than demonstrating reading, adds a timeline, a budget and a team case, and is written to a page limit that is enforced. Most clinical studies need both, and writing one from the other is a rewrite rather than a reformat. The commonest mistake is submitting a protocol to a funder: it reads as thorough and uncompetitive, because it never says why anybody should care."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-5"}><span>{"How do I align a proposal with a funding agency's requirements?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Read the call and the scoring criteria before writing anything, and write to the criteria in the order and with the weight the funder gives them. Horizon Europe scores Excellence, Impact, and Quality and Efficiency of the Implementation, in that order, and most clinical proposals lose marks on impact because they write a hope where a pathway is asked for. NIH reads the Specific Aims page first and reads everything after it in the light of that page, so it is written first and rewritten last; the data management and sharing plan has been required since the 2023 policy and is still routinely thin. NIHR wants patient and public involvement evidenced rather than asserted — who was involved, when, and what changed as a result — alongside a plain English summary that is genuinely plain. ICMR, DBT and DST prescribe their formats and their budget heads, and the forms fail more proposals than the science does. And every funder has page limits that are enforced by software rather than by goodwill."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-6"}><span>{"When do I have to register the trial?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Before the first participant is enrolled, and this is one of the few things in research that genuinely cannot be fixed later. The ICMJE requires prospective registration in a WHO primary registry or on ClinicalTrials.gov as a condition of consideration at member journals, and the registration date is public and permanent — so a trial registered after enrolment starts carries that fact forever, and it will be the first thing an editor sees years later when you submit the paper. Which registry depends on where you are: the Clinical Trials Registry – India, ClinicalTrials.gov in the United States, ISRCTN or ClinicalTrials.gov in the UK alongside Health Research Authority approval, and the EU Clinical Trials Information System under Regulation 536/2014 for trials running in member states. Register the outcomes you actually intend, in the order you intend them, because the registered record is what your eventual paper will be checked against for outcome switching."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-7"}><span>{"Is ICH-GCP still E6(R2)?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No. ICH E6(R3) is current: its Principles and Annex 1 were adopted by ICH and by the CHMP on 23 July 2025 and are described as a replacement for E6(R2). Annex 2, which covers pragmatic and decentralised trial designs, reached Step 4 in June 2026 and applies in the EU from 15 January 2027, with a consolidated version of all three parts published in July 2026. A protocol written in 2026 that still cites E6(R2) as the current standard is a year out of date, and it is a visible error to anybody in regulatory affairs. The practical difference is proportionality: R3 asks for quality management built around the risks that actually matter to participant safety and to the reliability of the results, rather than uniform procedure applied regardless of risk. For investigator-initiated studies that is usually good news, because it makes a monitoring plan proportionate to a low-risk study defensible rather than something to apologise for."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"rp-8"}><span>{"Can you guarantee ethics approval or a grant award?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"rp-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and we will not quote a success rate as though we could. Ethics approval is a committee’s judgement and a funding decision is a panel’s, and both are made by people who have not met us. What we can commit to is the thing that is actually in our control: a submission set that is complete, internally consistent, written to the committee’s own format and to the current versions of the frameworks that govern it, read by a second person against the committee’s checklist before it goes in. That turns administrative queries into substantive ones, and a substantive query is usually answerable by a chair’s action rather than another full meeting. We will also tell you when we think a design cannot answer its question, which occasionally ends an engagement before it starts. That is a better outcome than a well-written protocol for a study that should not run."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of a protocol."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A protocol needs a question behind it and a paper in front of it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"BEFORE THE PROTOCOL"}</b><em>{"the question and the design"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Experimental design"}</b><span>{"The study designed before it is run, so the protocol has something to describe."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Clinical literature review"}</b><span>{"The evidence that establishes the gap your study is filling."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"THE NUMBERS"}</b><em>{"power, and the analysis plan"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Biostatistics and programming"}</b><span>{"Sample size, the analysis plan, and the analysis when the data arrives."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/grant-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Grant writing"}</b><span>{"The competitive document the funder scores, as distinct from the protocol."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"AFTER THE STUDY"}</b><em>{"the paper it owes"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Physician manuscripts"}</b><span>{"The protocol converted into the paper, which is a rewrite rather than a reformat."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical and regulatory writing"}</b><span>{"Clinical study reports, investigator brochures and the rest of the document set."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on design and publication."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on structuring research and placing it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the idea. You get the feasibility answer before the quote."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"Whether the design can answer the question, what your submission set contains, how long it takes to assemble and whether your committee date is realistic — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
